issue_context.body:
Using build:
```
SDK 6.0.100-rc.1.21427.28
Host 6.0.0-rc.1.21426.17
Microsoft.AspNetCore.App 6.0.0-rc.1.21427.16
Microsoft.NETCore.App 6.0.0-rc.1.21426.17
```

1. Create an empty web project, e.g. `dotnet new web`
2. Add an `IHostingStartup` class to the project and register it via the assembly attribute:
  ``` c#
  [assembly:HostingStartup(typeof(MyHostingStartup))]
  namespace MyTestWebApp;
  public class MyHostingStartup : IHostingStartup
  {
      public void Configure(IWebHostBuilder builder)
      {
          var test = "Test string";
      }
  }
  ```
3. Debug the web project and ensure that `MyHostingStartup.Configure` is called
4. Add an xUnit test project to the solution, e.g. `dotnet new xunit`
5. Add a reference to the web project to the test project, e.g. `dotnet add reference Path/MyTestProject.csproj`
6. Set internals visible to in the web project so the test project can see internal types, e.g. in the MyTestWebApp.csproj file:
  ``` xml
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="MyTestWebApp.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
  ```
7. Add a test that uses `WebApplicationFactory` to send a request to the web project, e.g.:
  ``` c#
  using System.Net;
  using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing;
  using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
  using Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting;
  using Xunit;
  
  namespace MyTestWebApp.Tests
  {
      public class HostingStartupTest
      {
          [Fact]
          public async Task Root_Responds_OK()
          {
              await using var application = new MyWebApplication();
              
              var client = application.CreateClient();
              var response = await client.GetAsync("/");
  
              Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.OK, response.StatusCode);
          }
  
          class MyWebApplication : WebApplicationFactory<Program>
          {
              protected override IHost CreateHost(IHostBuilder builder)
              {
                  // Add mock/test services to the builder here
  
                  return base.CreateHost(builder);
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```
8. Debug the test and see that the `MyHostingStartup.Configure` method is not called
